DIAGNOSTIC: re-apply the receiver configuration with the sensor already emitting

WHY
---
There is a difference in ORDER with the vendor that had not been looked at:

    mainline      VFE -> CSID -> CSIPHY -> sensor
    Qualcomm      CSIPHY -> CSID -> sensor

In mainline, video_start_streaming() walks the chain from the video node towards
the sensor calling s_stream(1), so the CSID starts listening BEFORE the CSIPHY
is powered up, and well before the sensor emits.

If the receiver latches its interface with the PHY at the moment it starts,
doing it too early would leave it looking at a dead cable forever. And it fits
everything that was measured: the CSID configuration is CORRECT -read back on
stop: rx_cfg0=0x00132103, rx_cfg1=0x00000041, rdi_cfg0=0x802bf007,
rdi_ctrl=0x00000001- and even so it does not count a single packet.

WHAT IT DOES
------------
A parameter that, when written 1, re-applies __csid_configure_rx() and the RDI
start command, that is WITH THE SENSOR ALREADY TRANSMITTING.

That way the test does not depend on guessing a delay: capture is started, the
sensor is given time to be really emitting, and only then is it re-applied.

    packets start arriving      -> the fault is one of ORDER, and it is fixed
                                   by moving the receiver configuration to
                                   after the PHY start
    still nothing arrives       -> order is not it, and it is ruled out

This does NOT fix anything on its own: it is for deciding.
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-gen2.c	2026-08-17 12:58:26.885167533 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-gen2.c	2026-08-17 12:58:26.903814367 +0200
@@ -49,6 +49,31 @@
  * interrupciones por fotograma esto puede convertirse en una tormenta, y este
  * movil es sensible a la temporizacion. Se enciende a mano cuando haga falta.
  */
+/*
+ * REAPLICAR LA CONFIGURACION DEL RECEPTOR, A MANO Y CUANDO YO QUIERA.
+ *
+ * mainline arranca la cadena en este orden:  VFE -> CSID -> CSIPHY -> sensor
+ * y el fabricante en este otro:              CSIPHY -> CSID -> sensor
+ *
+ * O sea que aqui el CSID se pone a escuchar ANTES de que el PHY exista. Si el
+ * receptor engancha su interfaz con el PHY en el momento de arrancar, hacerlo
+ * antes de tiempo lo dejaria mirando a un cable muerto para siempre.
+ *
+ * Escribiendo 1 en este parametro se vuelve a aplicar la configuracion del
+ * receptor y la orden de arranque del RDI, con el sensor ya transmitiendo. Si
+ * entonces empiezan a llegar paquetes, el fallo es de orden.
+ */
+static struct csid_device *diag_csid_guardado;
+static int diag_reaplicar_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp);
+static const struct kernel_param_ops diag_reaplicar_ops = {
+	.set = diag_reaplicar_set,
+	.get = param_get_int,
+};
+static int diag_reaplicar;
+module_param_cb(diag_reaplicar, &diag_reaplicar_ops, &diag_reaplicar, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_reaplicar,
+	"Escribir 1 para reaplicar la configuracion del receptor con el sensor ya transmitiendo.");
+
 static unsigned int diag_pkts;
 module_param(diag_pkts, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_pkts, "Paquetes CSI-2 recibidos (contador de hardware, 0x160).");
@@ -244,6 +269,8 @@
 static void __csid_configure_rx(struct csid_device *csid,
 				struct csid_phy_config *phy, int vc)
 {
+	diag_csid_guardado = csid;
+
 	u8 lane_cnt = csid->phy.lane_cnt;
 	int val;
 
@@ -511,6 +538,27 @@
  *
  * Return IRQ_HANDLED on success
  */
+static int diag_reaplicar_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	struct csid_device *csid = diag_csid_guardado;
+	int ret, i;
+
+	ret = param_set_int(val, kp);
+	if (ret || !diag_reaplicar || !csid)
+		return ret;
+
+	dev_info(csid->camss->dev, "csid%d: reaplicando la configuracion del receptor\n",
+		 csid->id);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < MSM_CSID_MAX_SRC_STREAMS; i++)
+		if (csid->phy.en_vc & BIT(i)) {
+			__csid_configure_rx(csid, &csid->phy, i);
+			__csid_ctrl_rdi(csid, 1, i);
+		}
+
+	return 0;
+}
